  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe positioning feeds of a probe cycle (the descent from the rapid / safe plane to each touch's start, the bore entry to its centre, the rise back to the safe plane) were plain G01. They now post as protected moves: stop on contact and alarm if the stylus trips on the way.\n\n- **Stream:** `post::dump` marks every non-rapid straight move of a path that carries probing touches, other than the touches and their incremental back-offs, as a new `GUARD x y z F feed` record (`Record::Guard`, `probe_rec::GuardRec`, documented in `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md`). An arc or a feed with no rate in a probe path is refused with a WARN. The safe-plane rapids stay rapids.\n- **Engine:** the new `onProbeGuard` hook (properties `X Y Z Feed`, `StartX/Y/Z`). A script without it is refused by name, once per operation. There is no PRELUDE default, because a plain feed would be the silent wrong answer.\n- **Fanuc (`fanuc.cps`):** `G31 X.. Y.. Z.. F..`, then for each moving axis `IF[ABS[#506n-<end>]GT0.001]THEN#3000=3(PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING)`. This works because, with no skip signal, the skip position is the block end.\n- **Tormach PathPilot (`tormach.cps`):** `G38.3 X.. Y.. Z.. F..`, then `oN if [#5070 EQ 1]` / `(MSG, PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING)` / `M2` / `oN endif`, with O-words from 5001.\n- **Inverted axes (`invert.rs`):** a GUARD is mirrored like an absolute move.\n- **Viewer map (`posting.rs`):** a GUARD counts as one motion record.\n\nSources (behaviour only): Fanuc's published custom macro B / G31 skip documentation (#5061-#5063, #3000); the LinuxCNC G-code reference (G38.3, #5070, O-code conditionals, MSG); Tormach's PathPilot machine-code reference (G38.2-G38.5 and M2 supported).\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/probe_guard.rs`:\n  - `the_positioning_feeds_of_a_probe_path_are_marked_protected`: every mode; no plain feed left; GUARD count per mode; one record per move.\n  - `the_guard_record_round_trips_and_refuses_malformed_lines`\n  - `fanuc_writes_protected_moves_as_g31_with_a_contact_alarm`: new golden `nc/fanuc/probe_corner.nc`.\n  - `tormach_writes_protected_moves_as_g38_3_with_a_trip_test`: new golden `nc/tormach/probe_guard_moves.nc`. It pins the guard blocks only, because Tormach's touches are #362 / PR #376.\n  - `a_probing_post_without_on_probe_guard_is_refused_by_name`\n- Regenerated Fanuc goldens: `probe_bore_centre`, `probe_corner_negative`, `probe_edge_negative_x`. The only change is G01 → G31 + the alarm line.\n- `probe_op::the_posted_g31_z_is_the_tip_at_the_expected_contact` now tells touches from guards.\n- Gate: these camcraft-app binaries are green, all run on the final head: conformance, fanuc_post, inverted_axis_display, inverted_equivalence, inverted_post, per_op_files, post_not_judged, posting, probe_guard, probe_op, probe_pick, probe_reach, project_roundtrip, scripting, tormach_machines, tormach_post. All camcraft-post tests are green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real controller or PathPilot Hub run. The G38.3 / #5070 block and the Fanuc G31 alarm are checked against the documentation only.\n- Tormach probe-op end to end: Tormach has no `onProbeMove` on main, so this waits for #376.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- **#376 (Tormach G38.2):** my Tormach hook sits in its own section, away from #376's hunks. Its probe goldens will gain the G38.3 blocks.\n- **#360 (Haas / Mazak / Siemens):** those scripts need `onProbeGuard`, or their probe ops are refused by name once this merges.\n- **#465 (inverted probing):** `invert.rs` gets a separate Guard arm that mirrors without refusing, so it is covered by #465's translation.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/174-probe-protected-descent.md`.\n\nChangelog: Probe op positioning moves (descent, bore entry, rise) post as protected stop-on-contact moves that alarm on an unexpected trip: G31 + #3000 on Fanuc, G38.3 + #5070 on Tormach PathPilot; a probing post without `onProbeGuard` is refused by name.\n\nFixes #174\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
